\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The three staleness policies at a deliberately large lag budget (\texttt  {examples/run\_async}). All three converge to the same final reward on the reference domain; what differs is the cost. Guarded discards $\sim $85\% of its rollouts as stale ($\sim $5.1\,s wall-clock vs.\ $\sim $3.2\,s); Reflective recovers almost all of that would-be waste by rebasing and re-verifying instead of discarding. Ratios are the result --- absolute counts scale with the host.\relax }}{9}{figure.caption.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:staleness}{{4}{9}{The three staleness policies at a deliberately large lag budget (\code {examples/run\_async}). All three converge to the same final reward on the reference domain; what differs is the cost. Guarded discards $\sim $85\% of its rollouts as stale ($\sim $5.1\,s wall-clock vs.\ $\sim $3.2\,s); Reflective recovers almost all of that would-be waste by rebasing and re-verifying instead of discarding. Ratios are the result --- absolute counts scale with the host.\relax }{figure.caption.7}{}}
\newlabel{fig:staleness@cref}{{[figure][4][]4}{[1][9][]9}}
